  "description": "freshness.v1 §2.3, §2.5–§2.8: a resource's kind and merged annotations (read as horizons.json reads them), and the observations a reader made of one member -> the combined verdict. Each observation is judged in §2.7's order, then combined: fresh if any is fresh, else stale if any is, else unobservable if any is (the first one's reason), else not_asked (the first one's reason); with no observation at all, §2.7's steps 1, 2 and 4 still answer (no horizon: not_asked, no_horizon; an event or operation: not_asked, kind; no horizon in the value: unobservable, not_a_horizon), and a member with a horizon is unobservable, no_observation (0.2). Observations: {\"via\": \"subscription\", \"listened_s\": seconds since the subscription was declared, \"complete\": false when it lost deliveries, \"last\": null or {\"kind\": \"put\" | \"delete\", \"age_s\": seconds since that delivery, on the subscriber's monotonic clock}}; {\"via\": \"get\", \"reply\": null (no reply for the member) or {\"kind\": \"delete\"} or {\"kind\": \"put\", \"stamp_age_s\": the reader's clock minus the stamp's time, negative when the stamp is ahead, or null when the reply has no stamp}, \"clock\": {\"trusted\": false} or {\"trusted\": true, \"delta_s\": the delta the clocks are trusted to}}; {\"via\": \"archive\"}. expect.verdict is fresh, stale, unobservable or not_asked (a premise that does not hold, an event or a deleted member, is not_asked), and expect.reason its class: within_horizon, never_stale, beyond_horizon, no_delivery, not_a_horizon, listened_too_short, incomplete, silent, no_stamp, clock_untrusted, clock_disagrees, near_horizon, no_observation, no_horizon, kind, last_known, deleted. Seconds are compared exactly, to the nanosecond."
